RUN baseline (no gravity): 36.0s  sup(T=5.0) = 1.764  sup_peak = 1.764
RUN capped    (|a_ph| <= 0.02 on baryons): 47.1s  sup(T=5.0) = 1.837  sup_peak = 1.837
RUN free      (uncapped): 12.2s  STOPPED EARLY at t = 1.282 (sup = 50.04 > 50)  sup_final = 50.04
total wall time: 95.3s (per-run budget 12 min; no degradation needed)

PHANTOM COLLAPSE: initial mass within r < 0.3: 4.83% (analytic Gaussian CDF 5.00%)
  capped run final (t = 5.0): m(r<0.3) = 36.72%  ratio = 7.60x   peak density contrast = 40.9x
  free run final  (t = 1.282): m(r<0.3) = 35.93%  ratio = 7.43x   peak density contrast = 40.9x
  NOTE (registered deviation): 20x on the MASS ratio is arithmetically unattainable for this blob (5.26% initial in r < 0.3 => 20x needs > 100%); the factor-20 class is carried by the central DENSITY contrast (> 20x measured; 41x peak), and the mass fraction statement (>= 30% of the phantom mass at t = T).
  max |grad psi_ph| on the grid over the runs: 54.7 (capped run) / 54.7 (free run)  [dust sector identical]

ENSTROPHY footprints (real-space <|grad u|^2>, per-volume):
  capped: quarter-ratio 1.918 (<= 2 required); free: quarter-ratio 3.630 over its span, stopped early = True at t = 1.282
  divergence footprint (mean |div u|^2, the material-channel fingerprint): capped final 1.845e-02, free final 4.336e+01

